\f1 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ezekiel 33 has substantial material repeated from chapters 3, 18, and 24, and to a lesser extent other chapters. But Ezekiel often repeats; enough so we have adequate evidence he does so with a variety of purposes. So, I would like to start our discussion of Ezekiel 33 with the question, how, from what Ezekiel says, and how he says it, do we know what that purpose is in this case? For his purpose to have been accomplished, he needs to have left evidence in the text if we are careful to find it; his original audience of exiles needs to have been reachable along the lines of that purpose, so if we can reach sufficiently into that world, we can know Ezekiel's purpose.
\f0 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
